# XBD 6.1 Portable Character Set
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Run in the POSIX locale and in every locale that `locale -a` lists; the
# POSIX locale is always checked, so the test is never vacuous.

assertion  XBD.6.1-portable-character-set.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.1
class      required
since      1988
says       In the POSIX locale each of the 103 members of the portable
           character set is a complete one-byte character, the members have
           distinct encodings, the null character is the zero byte and every
           other member is a positive value as a char.
test       t/001-posix-single-byte.c

assertion  XBD.6.1-portable-character-set.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.1
class      required
since      1988
says       The encoded values of the digits 0 to 9 ascend by one in the
           POSIX locale and in every locale the system offers.
test       t/002-digits-ascend.c

assertion  XBD.6.1-portable-character-set.003
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.1
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.2
class      required
since      1988
says       Every locale the system offers includes the portable character
           set: each member is one byte that decodes back to the same
           character, the members are distinct and the null character is the
           zero byte.
test       t/003-every-locale-has-set.c

assertion  XBD.6.1-portable-character-set.004
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap06.html#6.1
class      required
since      1988
says       The encodings of period, slash, newline and carriage-return are
           the same in every locale: each is the value of its character
           constant and decodes to its own character.
test       t/004-four-invariant.c
